  message: "2026-11-01: now blocked by WI-fuzik-nogig-mizut-sudam-jasib-bobav-lavip-vidat (owner pre-approved). It measures whether the web-ingress verdicts are withheld for a principled reason or by accident (probes: flask/express route handlers writing a request value to disk read inconclusive only because the framework module is unclassified; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint_runnerup_11012026/), then adds an unseeded-ingress disclosure that names the handlers. This item then narrows that disclosure framework by framework as tier-1 seeding lands."  # 2bbf
- op: discuss  # 87fd
  at: '2026-11-02T08:52:53Z'  # 87fd
  by: agent  # 87fd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 87fd
  clock: 6  # 87fd
  nonce: 87fd  # 87fd
  message: "UNBLOCKED 2026-11-02: WI-fuzik is done (PR #2008). The disclosure half of ADR-0049 ruling 3 now exists for request handlers: verify_claims.unseeded_ingress_handlers(entrypoints) lists every entrypoint of an entrypoints.REQUEST_INGRESS_KINDS kind, and _withhold_for_unseeded_ingress withholds a clean untrusted_input taint verdict and a net_recv boundary verdict while any is listed (an already-inconclusive verdict gets the reason appended). CONTRACT FOR THIS ITEM: it deliberately lists EVERY handler, because nothing emits a seed marker yet. When this item seeds a framework's request carrier as an untrusted_input source, it must also NARROW that list for the handlers it seeded (same change, per ruling 3: removal only against a represented crossing), and the WI-fuzik tests must keep passing for a framework it does not seed. Measurement to reuse: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fuzik_step0_11022026/ (flip test + corpus before/after). Related residual: WI-jonin (Go ServeHTTP handlers are not entrypoints, so the list is empty on caddy)."  # 87fd
- op: discuss  # f71d
  at: '2026-11-03T11:35:34Z'  # f71d
  by: agent  # f71d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f71d
  clock: 7  # f71d
  nonce: f71d  # f71d
  message: "STEP 1 DONE 2026-11-03 (dev 3b6463d531): per-framework reach table in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/ritog_11032026/REACH.md (probes + inspect_reach.py + reach_probes.txt). Findings: (a) start_at:callee only relocates the BFS seed; the entry is still minted from a CALL EDGE into the callee, so a handler with no inbound edge (Flask, http.server, servlet, Go ServeHTTP) cannot be a callee-seeded source as the mechanism stands, and a structural seed at a handler would taint everything it reaches (reachability semantics, a false-positive machine for request handlers). (b) SERVLET: the accessor call carries its module slot (java:jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest:0-0:getParameter), so an ORDINARY caller-seeded net_recv source row matches today; no row exists in any catalogue (grep 0). Tier 2 should be rows, not a seed path. (c) FLASK: request.args.get lands as python:external:0-0:get with the receiver lost and no module_attr_ref edge: filed as WI-gabak-pulig-vugok-binud-lagat-somuz-napuh-nijor (P2); Flask becomes the servlet case after it. (d) EXPRESS: inbound dispatches_to exists but req.query.p is a member access (no edge) and JS records no parameters; GO: typed parameters ARE recorded (r *http.Request) but the accessor chain loses its receiver. Both need a DDG PARAMETER seed minted without a call edge: a taint/ddg design item of its own. (e) http.server reads self.path: no edge, hardest. Also available since WI-vumig (#2030): behavior_map['request_ingress'] = every request-handler symbol, uncapped, the same list the disclosure reads, so a seed and its narrowing can key on one list (caveat WI-rorug: the route-label dedup collapses distinct handlers). RECOMMENDATION (proceeding on 1-2 unless told otherwise; mode OFF/autonomous): 1. narrow unseeded_ingress_handlers by POSITIVE per-handler evidence: a handler leaves the list iff an untrusted_input source was minted with that handler as the CALLER (ADR-0049 ruling 3 'removal only against a represented crossing'; uniform across frameworks; a servlet reading req.getInputStream() with no row stays listed); 2. java io_primitives rows for javax/jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest accessors (getParameter, getParameterMap, getParameterValues, getHeader, getHeaders, getQueryString, getInputStream, getReader, getCookies, getPart, getParts) as net_recv sources, flip test on the servlet probe (untrusted-input-no-host-fs: inconclusive via the disclosure -> VIOLATED via the seed, handler leaves the disclosure); 3. Flask after WI-gabak-pulig-vugok-binud-lagat-somuz-napuh-nijor; Express/Go parameter seeding as a separate item."  # f71d
- op: discuss  # 2812
  at: '2026-11-03T15:10:03Z'  # 2812
  by: agent  # 2812
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2812
  clock: 8  # 2812
  nonce: '2812'  # 2812
  message: "STEP 2 SHIPPED in PR #2031 (merged; dev cb502dabd4). The item STAYS OPEN: Flask (WI-gabak first), Express/Go (DDG parameter seed: WI-sosov-rimuf-pifaz-kodas-bopus-vapud-tokub-zumol) and http.server are not seeded. SHIPPED: io_primitives_overlays/java-servlet.yaml, a COMMUNITY overlay (java.yaml is strict JDK stdlib) listing the javax/jakarta ServletRequest and HttpServletRequest value accessors as net_recv sources; taint.represented_ingress_callers (the CALLERS of matched untrusted_input sources from builtin or user-vouched rows, computed in the verify-claims loop from the propagator's own edge and source sets; a community row never counts, ADR-0061 ruling 2); verify_claims.unseeded_ingress_handlers(represented=...) skips those handlers (ADR-0049 ruling 3: removal only against a represented crossing), per handler, never per framework. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (production-path tests packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_servlet_ingress_evidence_narrowing.py, 6 cases; 4 mutations each red exactly the predicted set): with the shipped community rows the servlet probe's untrusted-input-no-host-fs goes VIOLATED through getParameter -> FileWriter while Saver.doGet STAYS in the disclosure on the other untrusted_input claims; the same rows supplied as a user overlay with --no-default-overlays: VIOLATED and Saver.doGet LEAVES the disclosure. CLI runs on the probe (lab ritog_11032026/RESULT.md, branch_summary.txt): default overlays: untrusted-input-no-host-fs violated via getParameter, Saver.doGet still named on the two other untrusted_input claims; user overlay + --no-default-overlays: violated and Saver.doGet absent (base: all three inconclusive, 0 flows, doGet named). P5 probe survey: entrypoints and request_ingress byte-identical (no detector change). P4 iceberg (via --input on the losij survey, generic claims): verdicts and evidence unchanged; the rows match S3SignerServlet.execute (getReader, getInputStream) and RESTCatalogServlet.ServletRequestContext.from (five listed accessors) through represented_ingress_callers, but no prohibited sink is reached and iceberg's servlets are not entrypoints (WI-hafib), so nothing was narrowed; getMethod is an unlisted accessor (candidate, not widened post hoc). WI-fuzik tests unchanged (flask/express/go handlers still named). CONTRACT GOING FORWARD: a framework is 'seeded' handler by handler, by a matched source call with the handler as caller; the narrowing never keys on a framework name or a marker nothing emits. NOT ASSERTED: that the accessor list is complete (request DATA accessors only; getSession/getRequestDispatcher/getRemoteAddr deliberately not listed); any effect on repos whose servlet calls lack the module slot."  # 2812
